8,What language family is Vietnamese? - 2026,https://theflatbkny.com/asia/what-language-family-is-vietnamese/,"Austro-Asiatic Once known as Annamese, Vietnamese is part of the huge Austro-Asiatic language tree. That means it comes from similar roots as Khmer in Cambodia and several other languages spoken by minority groups in the surrounding regions. Is Vietnamese based on French?",Muong,Austro-Asiatic
9,Vietnamese Linguistics: State of the Field,https://evols.library.manoa.hawaii.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/61ec98aa-1bcf-43fe-bd59-1ca9cf3829ec/content,Vietnamese belongs to the Viet-Muong sub-branch of the Vietic branch of the Austroasiatic language family. The dispersal of Austroasiatic languages in Mainland Southeast Asia is hypothesized to have begun in approximately 2000 BCE (Sidwell & Blench 2011).,Muong,Austro-Asiatic
